		<p class="csF0A1D375"><span class="cs5925EB86">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="csF0A1D375"><span class="cs5925EB86">METHODOLOGY:</span></p><p class="cs9E885863"><span class="csDD5E5F52">This bill, effective January 1, 2026, allows parents to send their children to public schools outside of their resident district, by making all New Hampshire public schools open enrollment schools. &nbsp;It is not possible to predict how many students may seek to enroll in a school outside their resident district, as allowed by this bill, and therefore it is not possible to predict this bill&#39;s impact on state aid programs, or local school district revenues or expenditures.</span></p><p class="csF0A1D375"><span class="cs5925EB86">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="csF0A1D375"><span class="cs5925EB86">AGENCIES CONTACTED:</span></p><p class="cs9E885863"><span class="csDD5E5F52">Department of Education</span></p><p class="csF0A1D375" style="tab-stops:left 18pt left 36pt left 54pt left 72pt left 90pt;"><span class="cs2C11128C">&nbsp;</span></p></body>
